// Old Kettil, capercaillie, town-mother of Kettil's Rest (bible 3.4, character-bibles.md §8).
// Voice (style guide 4): proverbs, orders, laughter; counts people out loud; never says "Guild" without spitting.
// Her image: the count. Rooms: Rest_1 (the gate), Rest_2 (the square). State she reads: the count, Brann, the
// debate, the walk, Hollowvein, the unlicensed flag.

title: Rest_Kettil
---
<<if not has_flag("emberdown.kettil.met")>>
    <<jump Rest_Kettil_First>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("boss.brann.defeated") and not has_flag("emberdown.kettil.brann")>>
    Kettil: The crane's gone down the stair. Counted him out myself. One, gone.
    Kettil: The furnace is cold for good. A town that can't be anchored by force. Remember that, Wren.
    <<flag emberdown.kettil.brann 1>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("emberdown.hollowvein.walked")>>
    Kettil: Thirty-one came up. We buried them in daylight. I counted every one, and I'll count them again tonight.
<<elseif has_flag("emberdown.hollowvein.buried")>>
    Kettil: The boards stay on. Some weights you carry by leaving them where they fell.
<<elseif has_flag("emberdown.debate.heard") and walk_known() and not has_flag("emberdown.hollowvein_opened")>>
    <<jump Rest_Kettil_Hollowvein>>
<<else>>
    Kettil: Six hundred and eleven at supper. Six hundred and twelve with you. Eat something.
<<endif>>
-> Who sings the roll-call?
    Kettil: Runa. My voice went in the smoke. Hers came out of it louder. Up the bell stair.
-> What's under the boards at the pit-head?
    Kettil: Hollowvein. Thirty-one of ours. Ask me again when you've heard the baths argue.
-> Nothing today.
    Kettil: Then go and be counted somewhere else. Ha.
===

title: Rest_Kettil_First
---
Kettil: Halt at the gate. One, two, and a stranger. You're the stranger.
Kettil: A stranger is a bird nobody remembers. Here, that's dangerous. For you, mostly.
<<if unlicensed()>>
    Kettil: And a cowl. A Guild cowl. She spits. Unlicensed, the reeds say. Better. Slightly.
<<else>>
    Kettil: And a cowl. A Guild cowl. She spits. Say you're not here to survey us.
<<endif>>
-> I'm here to go home. Halden.
    Kettil: Up the chimneys and over the ridge. Runa can teach you the wall. If she likes you.
-> The map sent me.
    Kettil: Maps don't send. Birds with maps send. We know which ones.
-> ...
    Kettil: Quiet. Good. The quiet ones get counted last and remembered longest.
Kettil: Supper's at dusk. Roll-call after, at the bell. Be there and you're one of the count.
<<flag emberdown.kettil.met 1>>
===

title: Rest_Kettil_Hollowvein
---
Kettil: You heard the baths. You know the numbers. And the reeds say you know the walk.
Kettil: Thirty-one under the pit-head. Buried standing. The families want them up.
Kettil: I kept the boards on because what's down there broke the mine.
-> Then let's bring them up.
    Kettil: Runa leads. You follow her count. Miss a name and you start the verse again.
    <<flag emberdown.hollowvein_opened 1>>
-> What broke the mine, Kettil?
    Kettil: A stone that wouldn't stay still. It hums. Ask it yourself, at the bottom.
    <<flag emberdown.hollowvein_opened 1>>
-> Leave the boards where they are.
    Kettil: Aye. That's a count too. I'll tell the families you said it, not me.
Kettil: The pit-head. Runa will be there before you.
===
